# ── Clerk (auth) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This zone's auth is CLIENT-ONLY: ClerkProvider plus the nav's prebuilt Clerk
# components run on the publishable key against the same-origin session that the
# parent glasskit.app app establishes. There are no protected routes here and
# nothing calls auth() server-side, so there is no clerkMiddleware and no secret
# key. See apps/web/proxy.ts.

# Publishable key for the SAME Clerk instance as the parent glasskit app —
# the shared session only carries over if both zones point at one instance.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_live_xxx

# REQUIRED IN PRODUCTION. Clerk's Frontend API domain, e.g. clerk.glasskit.app
#
# Why this is not optional: ClerkJS resolves its Frontend API host with an
# auto-proxy heuristic based on the domain it is served from. On a *.vercel.app
# host (every preview deploy, and production until a custom domain is attached
# to THIS project) that heuristic picks the wrong host, the /v1/client handshake
# never completes, and `useAuth().isLoaded` stays false forever. The symptom is
# a sign-in button that silently does not exist — see components/auth-button.tsx,
# which now degrades to a link to the parent zone after a timeout instead of
# rendering an invisible empty slot.
#
# Set this on the `glasskit-ui` Vercel project, not just locally.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_DOMAIN=clerk.glasskit.app

# ── Site ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Overrides the umbrella origin (default https://glasskit.app). Set it on a
# staging deploy so QR deep links point at that deploy instead of production —
# the glasses need a public HTTPS URL, so localhost is never useful here.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_ORIGIN=https://glasskit-ui-git-my-branch.vercel.app
